@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ca-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `ca-interpretation-calendar`

-- ca-tests-other.l4
--
-- Sections 30, 35(1) "month", 37, 39(1): the time module's remaining functions.
-- Expected values written from the text before the module was run.  Day counts and weekdays below were checked with a calendar
-- outside L4 (python3 `datetime`): 2024 has 366 days; the financial year beginning 2026-04-01 has 365 days and the one beginning
-- 2023-04-01 has 366; the 15th weekday after Saturday 2026-03-07 is Friday 2026-03-27.

GIVEN p IS A `A period`
      a IS A DATE
      b IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
p `runs from` a `to` b MEANS
        (p's `the first day`) EQUALS a
    AND (p's `the last day`) EQUALS b

§ `Section 30: the day a specified age is attained`

-- Born 15 March 2000: the 18th anniversary is 15 March 2018; not attained on the 14th, attained on the 15th and after.
#ASSERT `the anniversary of` 18 `years of the day of birth` (YMD 2000 3 15) EQUALS YMD 2018 3 15
#ASSERT NOT (`a person born on` (YMD 2000 3 15) `has attained` 18 `years of age on` (YMD 2018 3 14))
#ASSERT `a person born on` (YMD 2000 3 15) `has attained` 18 `years of age on` (YMD 2018 3 15)
#ASSERT `a person born on` (YMD 2000 3 15) `has attained` 18 `years of age on` (YMD 2018 3 16)
-- Born 29 February 2000: the 4th anniversary is 29 February 2004 (a leap year).
#ASSERT `the anniversary of` 4 `years of the day of birth` (YMD 2000 2 29) EQUALS YMD 2004 2 29
#ASSERT NOT (`a person born on` (YMD 2000 2 29) `has attained` 4 `years of age on` (YMD 2004 2 28))
#ASSERT `a person born on` (YMD 2000 2 29) `has attained` 4 `years of age on` (YMD 2004 2 29)
-- The 18th anniversary of 29 February 2000 would be 29 February 2018: no such day.  Section 30 does not send the reader to section 28.
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the anniversary of` 18 `years of the day of birth` (YMD 2000 2 29))
#ASSERT REFUSED (`a person born on` (YMD 2000 2 29) `has attained` 18 `years of age on` (YMD 2018 3 1))
-- Born 31 December 1999: the first anniversary is 31 December 2000.
#ASSERT `the anniversary of` 1 `years of the day of birth` (YMD 1999 12 31) EQUALS YMD 2000 12 31
-- A count that is not a whole number of at least one.
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the anniversary of` 0 `years of the day of birth` (YMD 2000 3 15))
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the anniversary of` 1.5 `years of the day of birth` (YMD 2000 3 15))

§ `Section 37(1): "year"`

-- (a) a calendar year: twelve consecutive months commencing on January 1.
#ASSERT (`the calendar year numbered` 2026) `runs from` (YMD 2026 1 1) `to` (YMD 2026 12 31)
#ASSERT `the number of days in` (`the calendar year numbered` 2026) EQUALS 365
#ASSERT `the number of days in` (`the calendar year numbered` 2024) EQUALS 366
-- (b) a financial year or fiscal year, in relation to money provided by Parliament or the finances of Canada: April 1 to March 31.
#ASSERT (`the financial year or fiscal year beginning in` 2026 `where` TRUE) `runs from` (YMD 2026 4 1) `to` (YMD 2027 3 31)
#ASSERT `the number of days in` (`the financial year or fiscal year beginning in` 2026 `where` TRUE) EQUALS 365
#ASSERT `the number of days in` (`the financial year or fiscal year beginning in` 2023 `where` TRUE) EQUALS 366
-- In any other relation the Act gives it no meaning.
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the financial year or fiscal year beginning in` 2026 `where` FALSE)
-- (c) a Dominical year by number: twelve consecutive months commencing on January 1 of that year.
#ASSERT (`the Dominical year numbered` 2026) `runs from` (YMD 2026 1 1) `to` (YMD 2026 12 31)
#ASSERT `the number of days in` (`the Dominical year numbered` 2024) EQUALS 366

§ `Section 37(2): the Governor in Council may prescribe which meaning a year has`

#ASSERT `the meaning prescribed under section 37(2)` TRUE TRUE (JUST `a financial year or fiscal year`) EQUALS `a financial year or fiscal year`
#ASSERT `the meaning prescribed under section 37(2)` TRUE TRUE (JUST `any period of twelve consecutive months`) EQUALS `any period of twelve consecutive months`
#ASSERT `the meaning prescribed under section 37(2)` TRUE TRUE (JUST `a period of twelve consecutive months commencing on January 1`) EQUALS `a period of twelve consecutive months commencing on January 1`
-- Nothing prescribed, or the conditions of the subsection not met: no prescription answers.
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the meaning prescribed under section 37(2)` TRUE TRUE NOTHING)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the meaning prescribed under section 37(2)` FALSE TRUE (JUST `a financial year or fiscal year`))
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the meaning prescribed under section 37(2)` TRUE FALSE (JUST `a financial year or fiscal year`))

§ `Section 35(1): "month" means a calendar month`

#ASSERT (`the calendar month containing` (YMD 2026 2 14)) `runs from` (YMD 2026 2 1) `to` (YMD 2026 2 28)
#ASSERT (`the calendar month containing` (YMD 2024 2 29)) `runs from` (YMD 2024 2 1) `to` (YMD 2024 2 29)
#ASSERT (`the calendar month containing` (YMD 2025 12 31)) `runs from` (YMD 2025 12 1) `to` (YMD 2025 12 31)
#ASSERT (`the calendar month containing` (YMD 2026 1 1)) `runs from` (YMD 2026 1 1) `to` (YMD 2026 1 31)
#ASSERT (`the calendar month containing` (YMD 2026 4 30)) `runs from` (YMD 2026 4 1) `to` (YMD 2026 4 30)
-- Twelve calendar months is a year under s 37(1): the twelve months after 2025-03-15 end on 2026-03-15.
#ASSERT ((`the period of` 12 `months after` (YMD 2025 3 15))'s `the last day`) EQUALS ((`the period of` 1 `years after` (YMD 2025 3 15))'s `the last day`)

§ `Section 39(1): laying a regulation before Parliament, with a sitting calendar the test supplies (Monday to Friday)`

-- Made on Monday 9 March 2026, a sitting day ("then sitting"): within fifteen days after it is made; the last day is 24 March.
#ASSERT `the last day for laying a regulation made on` (YMD 2026 3 9) `given the days the body sits` (GIVEN d YIELD NOT (`is weekend` d)) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 24
#ASSERT NOT (`the regulation made on` (YMD 2026 3 9) `may be laid on` (YMD 2026 3 9) `given the days the body sits` (GIVEN d YIELD NOT (`is weekend` d)))
#ASSERT `the regulation made on` (YMD 2026 3 9) `may be laid on` (YMD 2026 3 10) `given the days the body sits` (GIVEN d YIELD NOT (`is weekend` d))
#ASSERT `the regulation made on` (YMD 2026 3 9) `may be laid on` (YMD 2026 3 24) `given the days the body sits` (GIVEN d YIELD NOT (`is weekend` d))
#ASSERT NOT (`the regulation made on` (YMD 2026 3 9) `may be laid on` (YMD 2026 3 25) `given the days the body sits` (GIVEN d YIELD NOT (`is weekend` d)))
-- Made on Saturday 7 March 2026, not sitting: on any of the first fifteen days next thereafter that it is sitting, the 15th being Friday 27 March.
#ASSERT `the last day for laying a regulation made on` (YMD 2026 3 7) `given the days the body sits` (GIVEN d YIELD NOT (`is weekend` d)) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 27
#ASSERT `the regulation made on` (YMD 2026 3 7) `may be laid on` (YMD 2026 3 9) `given the days the body sits` (GIVEN d YIELD NOT (`is weekend` d))
#ASSERT `the regulation made on` (YMD 2026 3 7) `may be laid on` (YMD 2026 3 27) `given the days the body sits` (GIVEN d YIELD NOT (`is weekend` d))
#ASSERT NOT (`the regulation made on` (YMD 2026 3 7) `may be laid on` (YMD 2026 3 30) `given the days the body sits` (GIVEN d YIELD NOT (`is weekend` d)))
-- Not sitting on the day made: only a sitting day will do (Saturday 14 March is not one).
#ASSERT NOT (`the regulation made on` (YMD 2026 3 7) `may be laid on` (YMD 2026 3 14) `given the days the body sits` (GIVEN d YIELD NOT (`is weekend` d)))
-- Made on Sunday 8 March: the 15th sitting day after it is also Friday 27 March.
#ASSERT `the last day for laying a regulation made on` (YMD 2026 3 8) `given the days the body sits` (GIVEN d YIELD NOT (`is weekend` d)) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 27
-- A body that never sits: the search is bounded at 731 days (a bound of this encoding, not of the Act) and refuses.
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the last day for laying a regulation made on` (YMD 2026 3 7) `given the days the body sits` (GIVEN d YIELD FALSE))

§ `Section 28: three steps, as the section lists them`

-- (a) the month reached counting forward or backward, without including the month in which the day falls.
#ASSERT `the month index of` (YMD 2025 1 31) EQUALS 24300
#ASSERT `the month reached counting` 1 `months forward from` (YMD 2025 1 31) EQUALS 24301
#ASSERT `the month reached counting` 1 `months backward from` (YMD 2025 1 31) EQUALS 24299
-- (c) in that month, the day with the same calendar number, or the last day of the month.
-- The index is 12 times the year plus the month less one, so January 2025 is 24300, February 2029 is 24349 and December 2027 is 24335.
-- (The first draft of the last two rows below had the indices 24347 and 24323, a slip in my own arithmetic for the month wanted; the
-- expected days were kept and the indices were corrected to the months those days belong to.)
#ASSERT `the day counted in the month with index` 24301 `for a period counted from` (YMD 2025 1 31) EQUALS YMD 2025 2 28
#ASSERT `the day counted in the month with index` 24301 `for a period counted from` (YMD 2025 1 15) EQUALS YMD 2025 2 15
#ASSERT `the day counted in the month with index` 24302 `for a period counted from` (YMD 2025 1 31) EQUALS YMD 2025 3 31
#ASSERT `the day counted in the month with index` 24349 `for a period counted from` (YMD 2025 1 31) EQUALS YMD 2029 2 28
#ASSERT `the day counted in the month with index` 24335 `for a period counted from` (YMD 2025 1 31) EQUALS YMD 2027 12 31

§ `Section 28 agrees with the library's month arithmetic where the two overlap`

-- A cross-check, not a source of expected values: every one of these was decided from the text above.
#ASSERT ((`the period of` 1 `months after` (YMD 2025 1 31))'s `the last day`) EQUALS `add months` (YMD 2025 1 31) 1
#ASSERT ((`the period of` 1 `months after` (YMD 2024 1 31))'s `the last day`) EQUALS `add months` (YMD 2024 1 31) 1
#ASSERT ((`the period of` 12 `months after` (YMD 2024 2 29))'s `the last day`) EQUALS `add months` (YMD 2024 2 29) 12
#ASSERT ((`the period of` 6 `months after` (YMD 2025 8 31))'s `the last day`) EQUALS `add months` (YMD 2025 8 31) 6

§ `Section 39(1)(a) and (b): a regulation subject to affirmative resolution`

-- Not affirmed: it shall not come into force "unless and until" it is.
#ASSERT NOT (`a regulation subject to affirmative resolution can have come into force, given that` FALSE)
-- Affirmed: the text makes affirmation a condition and says nothing of the day, so no answer.
#ASSERT REFUSED (`a regulation subject to affirmative resolution can have come into force, given that` TRUE)
